/**
 * Day 92 — Phase 5 country pack 5, Southeast Europe: Greece refinement (ROADMAP item 5, last
 * country). The ancient Greek world (Bronze Age to Rome) is Day 56's (globe-greek-world.js) and
 * is not touched here.
 *
 * Before this, Greece between the end of the Byzantine ring (1025) and the Ottoman ring (from
 * 1500 on the mainland) was drawn only by Venice's two schematic boxes ('crete-foothold', which
 * grew over Crete from 800, and 'ionian-fringe', which covered Ioannina and Arta from 1345 to
 * 1630), Serbia's Dušan-era Epirus and Thessaly and Bulgaria's Aegean Thrace; the Ottoman ring
 * then covered Crete, the Ionian islands and Rhodes long before the Ottomans held them. Nothing
 * showed the Latin states of the Fourth Crusade, Epirus, Byzantine Mystras, the Knights of
 * Rhodes, Venetian Crete, Corfu or the Morea, or the Septinsular Republic. This pack adds 13
 * polities from 1194 to 1807. The nations layer draws Greece (id `greece`) from 1830; this pack
 * uses other ids and has no keyframe after 1813. Byzantine Greece after 1025, the Byzantine
 * provinces between the Latin states (Thessalonica 1246–1423, Thessaly 1333–1348), Genoese Chios
 * and Lesbos, Venetian Tinos and Ottoman Greece before the ring reaches it are timeline items with
 * pins, not outlines.
 *
 * How it is built (docs/DATA.md, "Country-pack globe backfill"):
 *  - 31 new pieces from Natural Earth 1:10m regions (public domain), clipped to the globe’s own
 *    close-zoom Greece land (nations-fine.topo.json shape 132). The Peloponnese and central
 *    Greece are cut along the Day 56 classical-region lines (globe-med-pieces.js: Achaea, Elis,
 *    Corinthia, Argolis, Arcadia, Laconia, Messenia, Boeotia), the Messenian peninsula south of
 *    36.97°N (Modon and Coron) and the Malea promontory east of 22.9°E (Monemvasia) are their
 *    own pieces, and Crete is cut at 24.93°E (Chania and Rethymno | Heraklion and Lasithi).
 *    Mainland pieces are cut back from the Serbia pack’s EPIRUS, THESSALY, W_MACEDONIA and
 *    North Macedonia and the Bulgaria pack’s E_MACEDONIA_THRACE so shared edges are noded once;
 *    EPIRUS, THESSALY and W_MACEDONIA are reused. Islands are the close-zoom land polygons, so the
 *    pack’s land check accepts the fine land. Generator: et-tools day92-pieces.py (outside the repo).
 *  - A polity is a dated list of pieces; every change is a one-year step.
 *  - Trims (`applyGreeceShapeFixes`, run after the Albania fixes): Venice’s schematic
 *    'crete-foothold' and 'ionian-fringe' regions are dropped (Venetian Crete, the Ionian islands
 *    and the Morea ports are polities here). The Ottoman `anatolia-balkans` ring is rebuilt as
 *    held steps from 1453 to 1813 (the 1453 → 1475 conquest morph in three-year steps), each split where
 *    this pack’s shapes change and cut back from them and from the Ionian islands after 1797
 *    (precomputed, buffered 0.05°, simplified 0.03°); cuts inside the ring are holes, like its
 *    Aegean Sea gap. The function throws if a source ring changes.
 *  - Pieces are regions, not surveyed borders (see each polity’s confidence reason).
 */

import { ensureClockwise, morphEntityAtYear } from './globe-morph.js';
import { resolveRegionHoles } from './globe-holes.js';
import { mergeRings } from './globe-med-pieces.js';
import { RS_PIECES } from './globe-pack-serbia.js';

const W = (title) => ({ title: `Wikipedia — ${title}`, url: `https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/${encodeURI(title.replace(/ /g, '_')).replace(/'/g, '%27')}` });

